  "worked_solution": "First we plot the graph of $y={(\\frac{1}{8})}^{x}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14239148/assets/f5d15cae5283eb02d555bee57f399dd00c58ec319413ca5817b1edba1ac69fb9.png)\n\nThen, we scale this graph by a factor of $\\frac{1}{2}.$ The $y$-intercept becomes $(0,\\frac{1}{2}),$ and the resulting graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14239148/assets/1b8e997035826ffcb6969c5bbdda46e256234fb5720f45aa281719be631929d4.png)",
